The cube_dump self-test compares the JSON output of cube_dump with a file
that was generated with GCC on x86_64. The JSON output prints every digit
of a double. With the Intel compilers 1520 of 2880 values differ in the
last digit, and the comparison fails. The self-test also fails with GCC
on ppc64le.

cube_dump still runs with "-s json" and the test still checks its exit
code. Only the comparison with the expected file is removed.

--- a/test/cube_dump/run_test.sh.in
+++ b/test/cube_dump/run_test.sh.in
@@ -279,14 +279,12 @@
 echo "=====> Select All Cnodes in human-readable Format..."
 ../cube_dump -m time -c all -z incl -t  0-10,25,27-30 -s json $CUBEFILE > cube_dump_print_json.out
 result22=$?
-diff cube_dump_print_json.out $TEMPLATE14_OUT
-result22_1=$?
+result22_1=0
 
 echo "=====> Select All Cnodes in human-readable Format..."
 ../cube_dump -m time -c all -z incl -t aggr -s json $CUBEFILE > cube_dump_print_json_aggr.out
 result23=$?
-diff cube_dump_print_json_aggr.out $TEMPLATE13_OUT
-result23_1=$?
+result23_1=0
 
 
 
